term: "Hybrid"
letter: "H"
anchor: "hybrid"
category: "general"
---

A cannabis strain that results from crossing indica-dominant and sativa-dominant plants. Virtually all modern cannabis strains are hybrids to some degree — the result of decades of selective breeding. At the dispensary, "hybrid" typically means a strain that doesn't fit cleanly into the indica or sativa box. The classification is less useful for predicting effects than examining a strain's specific cannabinoid and terpene profile.

→ [Indica vs. Sativa vs. Hybrid](/cannabis-101/indica-sativa-hybrid/)
